{
    "background_story": "Annie was a bright and ambitious high school student who had always been passionate about social justice. However, she noticed that many of her classmates struggled to afford menstrual products, leading to absenteeism and embarrassment. Determined to make a change, Annie founded a non-profit organization that provided free menstrual products to underprivileged schools in her community. She worked tirelessly to raise awareness and funds, eventually partnering with local businesses and government agencies to make her vision a reality. Annie's efforts not only improved the lives of countless young women but also helped to break down stigmas surrounding menstruation. Her dedication earned her recognition as a leading advocate for menstrual equity, inspiring others to join the movement.",
